  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "i6T/QuZlRhW3ZItZUjnbvi+/0/g=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:34.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## Six modes, one per invocation\n\n`ph connect config` reads and writes every `connect.*` field:\n\n```bash\nph connect config                                   # list the effective merged block\nph connect config connect.renown.url                # get (positional)\nph connect config --get connect.renown.url          # get (flag form, equivalent)\nph connect config connect.renown.chainId 137        # set (positional)\nph connect config --renown-chain-id 137             # set (per-field flag)\nph connect config --json '{\"drives\":{\"allowAddDrive\":false}}'   # bulk set\n```\n\nPositional `<key>/<value>`, `--get`, `--json`, and the field flags are **mutually exclusive** \u2014 combining them errors out. A positional `<value>` is JSON-parsed first (`137` \u2192 number, `false` \u2192 boolean) then Ajv-validated against the runtime schema at that path; bad types fail loudly *before* any write. Arrays and objects must go through `--json`.\n\n## The dual write\n\nA set or bulk-set patches two files:\n\n1. The **source** `powerhouse.config.json` at the project root, deep-merged into `connect.*` \u2014 so the next `ph connect build` inherits it.\n2. The **dist** `powerhouse.config.json` (default `.ph/connect-build/dist/`, overridable with `--dist-dir` or `PH_CONNECT_OUTDIR`), deep-merged the same way \u2014 so the currently-served SPA picks it up on its next refresh, no rebuild needed.\n\nIf the dist file does not exist the second write is skipped **silently** \u2014 that is the intended \"configure before the first build\" workflow, not an error.\n\nTwo gotchas. `--packages-registry` does not land under `connect.*`: it writes the top-level `packageRegistryUrl`, a project-wide field also read by `ph install`, `ph publish` and Switchboard. And `connect.pwa` is build-time only \u2014 `ph connect config` will happily write it but cannot rebuild the service worker, so PWA changes need `ph connect build`.\n\n`ph connect build` exposes the identical flag surface but has no read mode; passing `<key>` without `<value>` there errors out. Note a doc lag: the academy closes every config recipe with `ph service restart`, yet `service` is absent from the CLI's dispatch table (`phCliCommandNames`).\n\n_Source: `clis/ph-cli/src/services/connect-config.ts` and `apps/academy/docs/academy/03-Build/05-Launch/04-ConfigureEnvironment.md`, Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:35:34.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:34.000Z"
    }
  },
